msgid "Dev Services for Pulsar"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With Quarkus Messaging Pulsar extension (`quarkus-messaging-pulsar`)\n"
"Dev Services for Pulsar automatically starts a Pulsar broker in dev mode and "
"when running tests.\n"
"So, you don't have to start a broker manually.\n"
"The application is configured automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enabling / Disabling Dev Services for Pulsar"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev Services for Pulsar is automatically enabled unless:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.pulsar.devservices.enabled` is set to `false`"
msgstr ""

msgid "the `pulsar.client.serviceUrl` is configured"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"all the Reactive Messaging Pulsar channels have the `serviceUrl` attribute "
"set"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dev Services for Pulsar relies on Docker to start the broker.\n"
"If your environment does not support Docker, you will need to start the "
"broker manually, or connect to an already running broker.\n"
"You can configure the broker address using `pulsar.client.`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Shared broker"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Most of the time you need to share the broker between applications.\n"
"Dev Services for Pulsar implements a _service discovery_ mechanism for your "
"multiple Quarkus applications running in _dev_ mode to share a single broker."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you need multiple (shared) brokers, you can configure the `quarkus.pulsar."
"devservices.service-name` attribute and indicate the broker name.\n"
"It looks for a container with the same value, or starts a new one if none "
"can be found.\n"
"The default service name is `pulsar`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sharing is enabled by default in dev mode, but disabled in test mode.\n"
"You can disable the sharing with `quarkus.pulsar.devservices.shared=false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Setting the port"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, Dev Services for Pulsar picks a random port and configures the "
"application.\n"
"You can set the port by configuring the `quarkus.pulsar.devservices.port` "
"property."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that the Pulsar advertised address is automatically configured with the "
"chosen port."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuring the image"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dev Services for Pulsar supports the https://hub.docker.com/r/apachepulsar/"
"pulsar[official Apache Pulsar image]."
msgstr ""

